From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:32:29 -0300
Subject: Add --force-unreachable option for quorum testing

Some hosts sit behind a DDoS filter that breaks QUIC connections from
storage servers and session routers without blocking them entirely, so
they pass enough reachability tests to avoid ever being decommissioned
while still being unusable for much of the network.

--force-unreachable=IP[/MASK] (repeatable, and each value may be a
comma-separated list) makes this service node treat any node whose
public IP falls within one of the given ranges as failing, voting storage
server + lokinet + session router unreachable as the reasons.

The actual reachability stats reported over RPC are left untouched so
that they remain useful for judging whether the underlying problem still
exists; new *_forced_unreachable RPC fields report the override instead.
